# selftests-gap.list: the subset of Linux's KVM selftests that compares
# Rach2's KVM with Linux's at the same depth: under the testing PC's KVM, on
# the host-svm processor with two processors and 6 GiB, Rach2 as
# machine.kvm.selftests-nested boots it and Debian's Linux 6.12 as
# linux-corpus.sh boots it (Readme.md, Running). It has every program that
# selftests.list runs, without those the owner excluded, and gives the six
# that touch a gigabyte or more smaller sizes, so that each system runs it
# in under half an hour. The form is selftests.list's, and a NAME
# PROGRAM,ARG,... runs PROGRAM with the ARGs. EXPECT and LINUX are both
# Linux's result in that machine, so that corpus.sh fails Rach2 on the tests
# that differ from Linux's; REASON names the card of each gap with the Rach2
# code it points at, a gap inside a test both systems pass or skip, and why
# Linux fails or skips (dev-log/81-kvm/81-26.md).
#
# NAME EXPECT LINUX REASON
access_tracking_perf_test skip skip Linux: CONFIG_IDLE_PAGE_TRACKING is not enabled
coalesced_io_test pass pass
demand_paging_test,-b,64M pass pass
dirty_log_perf_test,-b,64M pass pass
dirty_log_test,-i,4 pass pass bitmap, clear-log and dirty-ring modes; the ring stops on full and on a kick, and the host collects and resets it
guest_print_test pass pass
hardware_disable_test pass pass
kvm_binary_stats_test pass pass
kvm_create_max_vcpus pass pass
kvm_page_table_test,-b,128M pass pass
max_guest_memory_test,-m,4 pass pass
memslot_modification_stress_test,-b,64M pass pass
memslot_perf_test fail fail both: the RW case outlasts the alarm(10) of host_perform_sync (memslot_perf_test.c:418-426) at this depth
pre_fault_memory_test pass pass
rseq_test pass pass
set_memory_region_test pass pass
steal_time pass pass
system_counter_offset_test pass pass
x86_64/amx_test skip skip Linux: Required XSAVE feature 'XFEATURE_MASK_XTILE_DATA' not supported
x86_64/apic_bus_clock_test pass pass
x86_64/cpuid_test pass pass
x86_64/cr4_cpuid_sync_test pass pass
x86_64/debug_regs pass pass
x86_64/dirty_log_page_splitting_test skip skip Linux: HUGETLB is not enabled in /proc/sys/vm/nr_hugepages; Rach2 skips at the same check, its /proc/meminfo having no HugePages_Total: HUGETLB is not configured in host kernel
x86_64/exit_on_emulation_failure_test pass pass
x86_64/fix_hypercall_test fail fail both: disable_quirk fails fix_hypercall_test.c:75, ret == -EFAULT, on Rach2 and on Linux 6.12 alike, since WSL's KVM beneath takes the nested guest's #UD itself and writes VMMCALL over its VMCALL (dev-log/84-locks/upstream.md); WSL's Linux 6.18.58 one level up passes it
x86_64/get_msr_index_features pass pass
x86_64/hwcr_msr_test pass pass
x86_64/hyperv_clock pass pass
x86_64/hyperv_cpuid pass pass
x86_64/hyperv_evmcs skip skip Linux: Requirement not met: kvm_cpu_has(X86_FEATURE_VMX)
x86_64/hyperv_extended_hypercalls pass pass
x86_64/hyperv_features pass pass
x86_64/hyperv_ipi pass pass
x86_64/hyperv_tlb_flush pass pass
x86_64/kvm_clock_test pass pass
x86_64/kvm_pv_test pass pass
x86_64/max_vcpuid_cap_test pass pass
x86_64/monitor_mwait_test skip skip Linux: Requirement not met: this_cpu_has(X86_FEATURE_MWAIT)
x86_64/nx_huge_pages_test,-t,887563923,-p,100,-r skip skip with the token and CAP_SYS_BOOT, as nx_huge_pages_test.sh runs it as root: both take KVM_CAP_VM_DISABLE_NX_HUGE_PAGES and skip at its first hugetlb slot (get_def_hugetlb_pagesz, lib/test_util.c:166-193), Linux with HugePages_Total 0 and Rach2, which has no hugetlb pages, with no such line in /proc/meminfo
x86_64/platform_info_test pass pass
x86_64/pmu_counters_test skip skip Linux: Requirement not met: host_cpu_is_intel
x86_64/pmu_event_filter_test pass pass
x86_64/private_mem_conversions_test skip skip Linux: Requirement not met: kvm_check_cap(KVM_CAP_VM_TYPES) & BIT(KVM_X86_SW_PROTECTED_VM)
x86_64/private_mem_kvm_exits_test skip skip Linux: Requirement not met: kvm_check_cap(KVM_CAP_VM_TYPES) & BIT(KVM_X86_SW_PROTECTED_VM)
x86_64/recalc_apic_map_test pass pass
x86_64/set_boot_cpu_id pass pass
x86_64/set_sregs_test pass pass
x86_64/sev_init2_tests skip skip Linux: Requirement not met: __kvm_has_device_attr(kvm_fd, KVM_X86_GRP_SEV, KVM_X86_SEV_VMSA_FEATURES) == 0
x86_64/sev_migrate_tests skip skip Linux: Requirement not met: kvm_cpu_has(X86_FEATURE_SEV); Rach2 skips earlier, at KVM_CAP_VM_MOVE_ENC_CONTEXT_FROM, which only SEV uses
x86_64/sev_smoke_test skip skip Linux: Requirement not met: kvm_cpu_has(X86_FEATURE_SEV)
x86_64/smaller_maxphyaddr_emulation_test skip skip Linux: Requirement not met: kvm_has_cap(KVM_CAP_SMALLER_MAXPHYADDR)
x86_64/state_test pass pass
x86_64/sync_regs_test pass pass
x86_64/tsc_msrs_test pass pass
x86_64/tsc_scaling_sync pass pass
x86_64/ucna_injection_test skip skip Linux: MCG_CMCI_P is not supported, skipping test
x86_64/userspace_io_test pass pass
x86_64/userspace_msr_exit_test pass pass
x86_64/vmx_pmu_caps_test skip skip Linux: Requirement not met: kvm_cpu_has(X86_FEATURE_PDCM)
x86_64/xapic_ipi_test pass pass
x86_64/xapic_state_test pass pass
x86_64/xcr0_cpuid_test pass pass
x86_64/xen_shinfo_test pass pass
x86_64/xen_vmcall_test pass pass
x86_64/xss_msr_test pass pass
